title: Economic Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: economic_policy_timer += 12; month_actions += 1; nationalize_budget = 4; nationalize_budget -= 1 if works_councils >= 2; nationalize_budget -= 1 if works_councils >= 3; nationalize_budget -= 1 if socializations + nationalization_progress >= 2
view-if: finance_minister_party == "PSOE" and economic_policy_timer <= 0 and economic_plan > 0
card-image: img/portraits/SchmidtRobert.jpg
go-to: economic_plan_menu
#subtitle: Policies to address the economic crisis.

= Economic Policy

The party has already settled on an economic plan. Now, as long as we hold the Finance Ministry, we have to implement it. [? if budget < 0: If our budget falls too far into the red, a capital strike will almost certainly be triggered. ?]

@economic_plan_menu

- @public_works
- @public_works_deficit
- @nationalize_1
- @nationalize_2
- @moderate_plan
- @moderate_plan_limited_budget
- @austerity
- @root: Do not implement the economic plan.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

# Area I (I-2): the public-works arm, revived. The plan's WTB/public-works path
# (economic_plan == 1, set once the UGT public-works plan is adopted via the
# labor-economist advisor's @plan branch) was deleted as dead code in G-2 because
# nothing set wtb_adopted. Area I restores the adoption path, so this arm is live
# again - reframed as Prieto's hydraulic/infrastructure public-works program.

@public_works
title: Fund the public-works program.
subtitle: -2 budget.
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget. [? if budget < 2 : We do not have the necessary budget. ?] [? if unemployed < 8 : Unemployment is low enough that job creation is not necessary. ?]
view-if: wtb_adopted == 1
choose-if: budget >= 2 and unemployed >= 8
on-arrival: budget -= 2; works_program += 1; unemployed -= 4 if unemployed >= 8; unemployed -= 1 if unemployed >= 25; inflation += 2; industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 8*(1-dissent); landless_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; radical_relation += 2; izq_rep_relation += 3; pce_relation -= 5 if in_popular_front; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 1; economic_growth += 2.4
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

We have opened the taps on the public-works program - the great hydraulic works, the roads, the rail lines. Money begins to circulate through the economy, and unemployment falls as the works absorb landless labourers and the urban jobless alike. Our republican partners take credit for a recovery plan they can defend to the middle class[? if in_popular_front :, though the <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> dismisses it as propping up a capitalism it would rather see collapse ?].

@public_works_deficit
title: Fund the public-works program through deficit spending.
subtitle: We will run a deficit to keep the works going.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if unemployed < 10 : Unemployment is low enough that we should not run a deficit. ?]
view-if: wtb_adopted == 1 and budget < 2
choose-if: unemployed >= 10 and budget >= -3
on-arrival: budget -= 2; works_program += 1; unemployed -= 4 if unemployed >= 10; inflation += 3; industrial_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 8*(1-dissent); landless_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; radical_relation -= 4; ceda_relation -= 4; capital_strike_progress += 1; pce_relation -= 4 if in_popular_front; economic_growth += 2.8
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

We press on with the public works even into deficit. Our republican partners are alarmed at the red ink and the orthodox economists warn of inflation, but the works go on and the jobless are put to work. The propertied classes mutter about fiscal recklessness.

@austerity
title: Look into potential austerity measures.
subtitle: We have to scrounge up money somehow.
view-if: black_thursday_seen

- @cut_salaries
- @capital_levy
- @economic_plan_menu: Go back.

@cut_salaries
title: Slash the salaries of government employees.
subtitle: This will radicalize the middle class. +1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: We've already cut their wages.
choose-if: not government_salaries_cut
on-arrival: government_salaries_cut = 1; urban_middle_psoe -= 8; urban_middle_izq_rep -= 4; urban_middle_radical -= 4; urban_middle_falange += 12; pro_republic -= 5; labor_dissent += 15; left_dissent += 15; center_dissent += 10; unemployed += 1; inflation -= 0.5; economic_growth -= 0.4; budget += 1; radical_relation -= 15; izq_rep_relation -= 10; ceda_relation -= 6
go-to: austerity

We have slashed wages for government employees by about 15 percent, framing it as a painful but necessary step toward the Republic's economic recovery. The justification persuades few, and a portion of the middle class turns instead toward the authoritarian right.

@capital_levy
title: Impose a special levy on capital.
subtitle: A one-time tax on large fortunes and idle capital. Employers and the propertied classes will be displeased. +1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: We've already imposed the levy.
choose-if: not industrial_levy
on-arrival: industrial_levy = 1; reformist_dissent += 10; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; urban_middle_psoe -= 4; urban_middle_izq_rep -= 2; urban_middle_falange += 6; smallholder_psoe -= 4; smallholder_izq_rep -= 2; smallholder_falange += 6; pro_republic -= 3; capital_strike_progress += 3; unemployed += 1; inflation -= 0.8; economic_growth -= 0.8; upper_tax_rates += 1; budget += 1; radical_relation -= 15; izq_rep_relation -= 8; ceda_relation -= 5; president_angry += 20
go-to: austerity

We have imposed a special levy on large fortunes and idle capital. As expected, we have earned the ire of the business community[? if president == "Alcalá-Zamora": , who will take their complaints to President Alcalá-Zamora?]. Industrialists and landowners respond by doubling their financial support for the CEDA and the monarchist right, hoping they can bring down our government.


####################### left economic policies (socializations)

@nationalize_1
title: Implement the Left plan for the transformation of the economy.
subtitle: -[+ nationalize_budget +] budget. [? if works_councils >= 3 : Our factory committees have reduced the budget necessary for this program. ?] [? if socializations >= 2: Our existing socialization policies have reduced the budget necessary for this program. ?]
view-if: nationalization_adopted == 1 and nationalization_progress == 0
go-to: nationalize_deficit if budget < nationalize_budget; nationalize_no_deficit if budget >= nationalize_budget


@nationalize_no_deficit
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 2; unemployed -= 3.5 if unemployed >= 6; unemployed -= 1.2 if works_councils >= 3; budget -= nationalize_budget; works_program += 1; industrial_psoe += 8*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; radical_relation -= 4; izq_rep_relation -= 4; left_dissent -= 5; urban_middle_psoe -= 2; smallholder_psoe -= 3; inflation += 2; economic_growth += 1.7 if economic_growth < 5
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

[? if nationalization_progress == 1 : We have begun purchasing idling enterprises from their owners[? if works_councils >= 1: , and running them in coordination with empowered factory committees ?]. By keeping production going, we can stave off rising unemployment. ?]

[? if nationalization_progress == 1 : The Caballerista left argues that this should only be a first step in the socialist transformation of the economy. Eventually, much of the economy must be brought under popular control. ?]

[? if nationalization_progress > 1 : We purchase additional underutilized enterprises and run them in coordination with the factory committees, hiring formerly laid-off workers. A significant portion of the economy is now under public control. ?]

@nationalize_deficit

We do not have the budget to begin buying out industrial facilities. Some argue for deficit spending to purchase factories, while others push for (currently illegal) factory takeovers by the unions, or nationalization without compensation. Taking any of these actions would mean a sharp break from the party's previous, more cautious course.

- @nationalize_deficit_1
- @nationalize_without_compensation
- @empower_workers
- @return: No, we should not do this.


@nationalize_deficit_1
title: Take a budget deficit to fund the nationalization program.
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength + center_strength
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength + center_strength: The party does not yet support budget deficits for this purpose. ?]
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 3; unemployed -= 3 if unemployed >= 6; unemployed -= 1.2 if works_councils >= 3; budget -= nationalize_budget; works_program += 1; industrial_psoe += 8*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; radical_relation -= 6; izq_rep_relation -= 6; urban_middle_psoe -= 3; smallholder_psoe -= 3; inflation += 3; economic_growth += 2 if economic_growth < 5
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

[? if nationalization_progress == 1 : We have begun purchasing idling enterprises from their owners[? if works_councils >= 1: , and running them in coordination with empowered factory committees ?]. By keeping production going, we can stave off rising unemployment. ?]

[? if nationalization_progress == 1 : The Caballerista left argues that this should only be a first step in the socialist transformation of the economy. ?]

[? if nationalization_progress > 1 : We purchase additional underutilized enterprises, hiring formerly laid-off workers. A significant portion of the economy is now under public control. ?]

@nationalize_without_compensation
title: Nationalize without compensation.
subtitle: There is no reason we should not simply take over idle factories. This is likely to provoke a confrontation with the propertied classes.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength + center_strength: The bulk of the party does not support this quasi-legal action. ?] [? if judicial_reform < 3 : The judiciary would oppose this action. ?]
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength + center_strength and judicial_reform >= 3
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 7; coup_progress += 3; unemployed -= 2.5 if unemployed >= 6; unemployed -= 1.2 if works_councils >= 3 and unemployed >= 3; works_program += 1; industrial_psoe += 8*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 6*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; radical_relation -= 10; ceda_relation -= 8; izq_rep_relation -= 8; left_strength += 15; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent -= 10; urban_middle_psoe -= 5; smallholder_psoe -= 8; pce_relation += 5*(1-dissent); inflation += 4; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth < 4
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

The propertied classes are, predictably, up in arms about nationalization without compensation. They call it illegal expropriation, and it is. Nevertheless, idle factories serve no one, and we judge that radical action is called for.

[? if nationalization_progress == 1 : We have begun acquiring idling enterprises[? if works_councils >= 1: , and running them in coordination with empowered factory committees ?]. By keeping production going, we can stave off rising unemployment. ?]

[? if nationalization_progress > 1 : We acquire additional underutilized enterprises, hiring formerly laid-off workers. A significant portion of the economy is now under public control. ?]

@empower_workers
title: Empower workers to take over factories.
subtitle: We can promise to legalize factory occupations, giving the factories over to the unions. This is highly confrontational, and would likely provoke a reaction from the far right as well as the propertied classes.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength + neorevisionist_strength : The bulk of the party does not support this radical action. ?] [? if judicial_reform < 3 : The judiciary would oppose this action. ?] [? if ugt_militia_militancy < 0.25 : If we increased the militancy of the UGT Militia, perhaps we could do this. ?] [? if works_councils < 1 : We need the support of the factory committees first. ?]
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength + neorevisionist_strength and (judicial_reform >= 3 or ugt_militia_militancy >= 0.25) and works_councils >= 1
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 6; coup_progress += 5; unemployed -= 3 if unemployed >= 6; unemployed -= 1.5 if works_councils >= 3 and unemployed > 4; works_program += 1; industrial_psoe += 10*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 10*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; radical_relation -= 10; ceda_relation -= 8; izq_rep_relation -= 8; industrial_falange -= 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_falange -= 5*(1-dissent); left_strength += 15; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent -= 10; urban_middle_psoe -= 5; smallholder_psoe -= 10; factory_takeovers += 1; pce_relation += 5*(1-dissent); inflation += 3; economic_growth += 1 if economic_growth < 3
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

The propertied classes are, predictably, up in arms about legalizing factory occupations. They call it illegal expropriation, and it is. Nevertheless, we judge that radical action is called for.

The Falange and other far-right elements have been taking increasingly violent action around the occupied factories, calling the workers thieves and looters. But some working-class sympathizers of the far right are peeled away by the sight of it, or at least those with a residual sense of class solidarity.


@nationalize_2
title: Continue the Left plan for the transformation of the economy.
subtitle: -[+ nationalize_budget +] budget. [? if works_councils >= 3 : Our factory committees have reduced the budget necessary for this program. ?] [? if socializations + nationalization_progress >= 2: Our existing socialization policies have reduced the budget necessary for this program. ?]
view-if: nationalization_adopted == 1 and nationalization_progress >= 1
go-to: nationalize_deficit if budget < nationalize_budget; nationalize_no_deficit if budget >= nationalize_budget

#######################################
# Moderate economic plan

@moderate_plan
title: Implement the Prietista job-creation plan.
subtitle: -2 budget.
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget. [? if budget < 2 : We do not have the necessary budget. ?] [? if unemployed < 8 : Unemployment is low enough that job creation is not necessary. ?]
view-if: moderate_plan_adopted == 1
choose-if: budget >= 2 and unemployed >= 8
on-arrival: budget -= 2; works_program += 1; unemployed -= 3 if unemployed >= 8; unemployed -= 2 if unemployed >= 30; inflation += 1.5; industrial_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); moderate_plan_progress += 1; inflation += 1 if unemployed < 10; radical_relation += 3; izq_rep_relation += 3; pce_relation -= 5 if in_popular_front; economic_growth += 1.6
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

[? if moderate_plan_progress == 1 : We have started to implement the job-creation plan! Funds are sent to build public works - roads, irrigation canals, rail lines - across the country, reducing unemployment. ?]

[? if moderate_plan_progress > 1 : We have continued to fund the job-creation plan, building public works throughout the country. ?]

[? if unemployed >= 10 : Our republican coalition partners approve of this plan as the "least bad" alternative, seeing it as necessary to save the country's economy. ?]

[? if unemployed < 10 : Unemployment is low enough that the plan does not seem to have its intended effect. ?]

[? if in_popular_front: The <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> opposes the plan, seeing it as a rescue of capitalism rather than a step toward real <span style="color: #9b0000;">socialism</span>. ?]

@moderate_plan_limited_budget
title: Partially implement the Prietista job-creation plan, at a lower cost.
subtitle: -1 budget.
unavailable-subtitle: -1 budget. [? if budget < 1 : We do not have the necessary budget. ?] [? if unemployed < 8 : Unemployment is low enough that job creation is not necessary. ?]
view-if: moderate_plan_adopted == 1
choose-if: budget >= 1 and unemployed >= 8
on-arrival: budget -= 1; works_program += 1; unemployed -= 1 if unemployed >= 8; unemployed -= 2 if unemployed >= 30; inflation += 1; industrial_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); urban_middle_psoe += 1.5*(1-dissent); smallholder_psoe += 1*(1-dissent); moderate_plan_progress += 1; inflation += 1 if unemployed < 10; radical_relation += 1; izq_rep_relation += 1; pce_relation -= 5 if in_popular_front; economic_growth += 0.7
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

[? if moderate_plan_progress == 1 : We have started to implement the job-creation plan! Funds are sent to build public works across the country, reducing unemployment. ?]

[? if moderate_plan_progress > 1 : We have continued to fund the job-creation plan, building public works throughout the country. ?]

[? if unemployed >= 10 : Our republican coalition partners approve of this plan as the "least bad" alternative. ?]

[? if unemployed < 10 : Unemployment is low enough that the plan does not seem to have its intended effect. ?]

[? if in_popular_front: The <span style="color: #700000;">**PCE**</span> opposes the plan, seeing it as a rescue of capitalism rather than a step toward real <span style="color: #9b0000;">socialism</span>. ?]
